{
  "language": "javascript",
  "runner": "node --test (node:test built-in, Node >=22; invoked through the repo's own wrapper scripts/hermetic.mjs)",
  "typecheck": {
    "cmd": "tsc",
    "args": ["--noEmit"],
    "cwd": null,
    "env": {},
    "source": "package.json scripts.typecheck = \"tsc --noEmit\"; tsconfig.json sets allowJs+checkJs+strictNullChecks(not full strict), include [\"src/**/*.js\"], exclude [\"types\",\"node_modules\"], declaration/emitDeclarationOnly/declarationDir ./types; .github/workflows/ci.yml runs `npm run typecheck` then `npm run build:types` (`tsc`) before `npm test`",
    "inferred": false
  },
  "test": {
    "cmd": "node",
    "args": ["scripts/hermetic.mjs", "&&", "node", "scripts/prompt-commit-check.mjs", "--range", "origin/main..HEAD"],
    "cwd": null,
    "env": {
      "PROMPT_COMMIT_RANGE": "origin/main..HEAD (optional; when unset the script falls back to --range origin/main..HEAD, and to HEAD~1..HEAD if that range does not resolve)"
    },
    "source": "package.json scripts.test = \"node scripts/hermetic.mjs && node scripts/prompt-commit-check.mjs --range origin/main..HEAD\"; scripts/hermetic.mjs spawns process.execPath with ['--test', ...argv] and rewrites HOME/GIT_CONFIG_*/GIT_AUTHOR_*/GIT_COMMITTER_*/EMAIL; .github/workflows/ci.yml sets PROMPT_COMMIT_RANGE on push events",
    "inferred": true
  },
  "envNeeds": [
    {
      "name": "PROMPT_COMMIT_RANGE",
      "value": "<before-sha>..<after-sha>",
      "why": "Optional override read by scripts/prompt-commit-check.mjs (CI sets it on push events so every commit of a multi-commit push is checked). When unset the script falls back to the --range argument origin/main..HEAD, then to HEAD~1..HEAD; if `origin/main` does not exist (fresh/detached clone) the check SKIPS rather than fails, so the prompt-register guard silently does nothing. Not required for type-checking or for the node --test run to parse."
    },
    {
      "name": "HOME",
      "value": "<fresh empty temp dir — scripts/hermetic.mjs sets this itself>",
      "why": "Set by the test wrapper to an empty mkdtemp directory so no ~/.gitconfig or ~/.npmrc leaks into tests (F136). Do not pre-set or override it: a real HOME is what made three releases go red only on CI. GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 are also forced by the wrapper, and inherited GIT_AUTHOR_*/GIT_COMMITTER_*/EMAIL are deleted."
    },
    {
      "name": "NODE_TEST_CONTEXT",
      "value": "<must be unset when invoking scripts/hermetic.mjs directly>",
      "why": "If set, scripts/hermetic.mjs refuses to run (exit 1) because that means it was discovered as a test file by node --test and would nest a second suite. tests/hermetic-args.test.js deletes it before spawning the wrapper. Irrelevant when PATH is left inherited."
    }
  ],
  "sourcePaths": ["src/", "bin/bareloop.mjs"],
  "testPaths": ["tests/", "tests/fixtures/"],
  "extensions": [".js", ".mjs"],
  "outputShapes": {
    "typecheckErrorLine": "src/backup.js(21,19): error TS7006: Parameter 'now' implicitly has an 'any' type.",
    "testSummaryLine": "# tests 317",
    "inferred": false
  },
  "layout": "Single-package, pure-ESM JS library (`\"type\": \"module\"`) with no build step for shipped code: JSDoc-only types, `src/` (flat, ~150 modules plus `src/panel/`), `bin/bareloop.mjs`, a flat `tests/` directory of ~700 node:test files supported by shared harness modules (helpers.js, *-world.mjs, *-fixtures.js) and tests/fixtures/. Types are generated into git-ignored `types/` using `tsc` with `emitDeclarationOnly`. Alongside the library sit `scripts/`, `experiments/`, `poc/`, `jobs/`, `design/`, `docs/` and a large `node_modules/`, but tsconfig only includes `src/**/*.js`.",
  "notes": [
    "TS config is deliberately NOT full strict: `strict: false` with `strictNullChecks: true`. CLAUDE.md forbids `!`, `as any` and `@ts-ignore`; the CI 'no-suppressions' close stage also flags `/** @type {T} */ (x)` casts.",
    "tsconfig excludes tests: a type error introduced only in tests/ will NOT be caught by `npm run typecheck`. Only `src/` is checked and only `src/` emits declarations.",
    "`npm test` is two steps, and the second one gates on git history: after the node --test suite passes, scripts/prompt-commit-check.mjs validates that any commit touching src/promptregisters.js carries Failure/Addresses/Corrects labels (Failure must cite `run <id>`). It exits non-zero on violation and prints a one-line summary otherwise. A raw `node --test` run bypasses both the hermetic HOME sandbox and this check.",
    "Pass a test path to the wrapper, not to node directly: `node scripts/hermetic.mjs tests/foo.test.js`. scripts/hermetic.mjs refuses a non-existent path-looking argument ('no such test path: …') instead of letting node --test silently skip it.",
    "scripts/hermetic.mjs must never be renamed onto one of node's default test-file globs (test-*.js etc.) or node --test will discover and run it as a test (documented F136 regression). test discovery otherwise relies on node's defaults — there is no --test glob or config file in package.json.",
    "Always `actions/checkout` with fetch-depth: 0 in CI — tests/close-stages.test.js reads history via `git show <sha>:…` and silently skips on a shallow clone. Expect the suite to need full git history locally too.",
    "litectx's impact() shells out to ripgrep; the two ctx_impact tests need `rg` on PATH (CI installs it explicitly). PATH, node_modules and network are NOT neutralised by the hermetic wrapper.",
    "Node reporter output is TAP only when stdout is not a TTY; fixtures and tests parse `^# tests (\\d+)$` / `^# fail (\\d+)$` / `# duration_ms …`, and a green run still prints `# fail 0`. Grading/parsing that relies on these lines must pipe stdout.",
    "`npm run build:types` (`tsc` with emitDeclarationOnly) is a separate CI step; `types/` is git-ignored and must never be hand-edited (generated on publish via prepublishOnly).",
    "Also present but not part of typecheck/test: `npm run check:lockfile` (scripts/check-lockfile.mjs), and a large `scripts/` set of experiment/probe/battery drivers (run-battery-*.mjs, *-close.mjs) that are operator tooling, not the test suite. No lint step exists by design."
  ]
}
